      "gds": "",
      "title": "A digital twin of pancreatic islet differentiation enables predictive modeling of cell fate",
      "summary": "Understanding cell fate specification during in vitro differentiation is critical to ensure stem cell-derived islet organoids become a viable cure for diabetes. Despite significant insights gained from single-cell sequencing technologies, the field lacks a predictive framework to resolve cell fate specification and infer the regulatory determinants of lineage trajectories. Here, we present a digital twin of in vitro pancreatic islet differentiation that not only characterizes cell-state-specific regulatory dynamics during in vitro differentiation, but also enables predictive assessment of candidate lineage specification regulators. Within this framework, we perform and verify in silico simulations to determine drivers of cell fate at critical developmental points. These results establish a digital twin framework for SC-islet differentiation and provide a foundation for improving in vitro biomanufacturing processes.",
